{
  "_comment": "Live config. Put your best model on unify - it writes the book. The editor must be a different model from unify, or it will approve its own work. A role's value can be a single {provider, model, ...} dict, or a LIST of them - a fallback chain tried in preference order, falling back only once a candidate's own internal retries are fully exhausted (see providers.call_model). Useful when one provider has a bad night: list your best model first, a more available one next, then a wholly different provider as a last resort. Pin '-latest'-style aliases where a provider offers them (e.g. mistral-small-latest) rather than a dated snapshot - it costs nothing and avoids the exact version-churn problem that broke several pinned models in this project's own history. Groq is deliberately absent from the heavy roles' chains (action/character/atmosphere/unify/editor) - live proof it can't serve them: a large canon.md + motif-ledger payload hit a 413 'tokens per minute (TPM): Limit 8000' even on a bigger Groq model, so it's kept only on skeleton/summariser, whose payloads stay genuinely small. Cerebras's model is gpt-oss-120b, not a Llama model - an earlier llama3.3-70b entry died with a live 404 'model_not_found' once it was actually reached (Cerebras had deprecated it account-wide by then), crashing the run since it was the last candidate in the chain with nowhere further to fall back to. Also: never push a new commit to main while a scheduled run is in progress - its own end-of-run checkpoint push can get rejected as a non-fast-forward conflict, silently losing that run's work.",

